<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zürich Oberland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zurich Oberland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zürich Oberland is the hilly eastern part of the canton of Zürich, around the towns of Wetzikon, Hinwil and Bauma. From the seventeenth century its households spun and wove <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> for city merchants, and in the nineteenth century water-powered factories spread along its streams. In 1832 hand-weavers burned a mechanised mill in the Usterbrand.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zurich-oberland.jpg" alt="Zürich Oberland" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Berger~commonswiki assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HinwilBachtel.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
